- I need you to get the fuck out . - I 'm so sorry .

523
00:29:27,037 --> 00:29:28,203
- Sam . - Please .

524
00:29:28,337 --> 00:29:30,339
Get the fuck out !

525
00:29:37,313 --> 00:29:39,782
[ door opens , closes ]

526
00:29:44,821 --> 00:29:46,455
[ cries ]

527
00:29:48,925 --> 00:29:52,227
- [ gasps ] - Hey , hey . It 's okay , it 's me .

528
00:29:53,997 --> 00:29:55,664
Were you listening at the door ?

529
00:29:56,298 --> 00:29:58,200
No , no , of course not .

530
00:29:59,134 --> 00:30:01,604
Okay , yeah , I was listening at the door .

531
00:30:02,204 --> 00:30:03,739
It doesn 't freak you out ...

532
00:30:04,607 --> 00:30:06,876
that my real father was a serial killer ?

533
00:30:07,576 --> 00:30:08,677
I mean ...

534
00:30:09,144 --> 00:30:10,446
yeah .

535
00:30:10,981 --> 00:30:12,348
A great deal , yeah .

536
00:30:12,481 --> 00:30:15,384
Okay , well , then go . I get it .

537
00:30:16,585 --> 00:30:18,454
I just got to stay and figure it out .

538
00:30:18,587 --> 00:30:20,356
I 'm not leaving you here , Sam .

539
00:30:21,390 --> 00:30:22,892
You know that part in horror movies

540
00:30:23,026 --> 00:30:25,194
where you want to yell at the characters to be smart

541
00:30:25,327 --> 00:30:26,896
and get the fuck out ?

542
00:30:27,964 --> 00:30:30,332
This is that part , Richie .

543
00:30:30,466 --> 00:30:32,368
You should get the fuck out .

544
00:30:36,405 --> 00:30:37,640
But I 'm staying .

545
00:30:41,176 --> 00:30:42,611
I love you .

546
00:30:46,983 --> 00:30:50,552
- You 're such a dumbass . - I 'm such a dumbass .

547
00:30:51,787 --> 00:30:52,956
So ...

548
00:30:53,089 --> 00:30:55,290
your sister won 't talk to you .

549
00:30:56,059 --> 00:30:57,861
The police aren 't gonna help .

550
00:30:57,994 --> 00:30:59,628
What 's our next move ?

551
00:31:02,164 --> 00:31:03,867
We go talk to an expert .

552
00:31:04,333 --> 00:31:06,368
[ birds chirping ]

553
00:31:06,502 --> 00:31:09,806
[ weather reporter ] ... temperatures here Tuesday , Wednesday in the mid-50s ,

554
00:31:09,939 --> 00:31:12,876
and then finally we 'll see those mid-60s returning next week .

555
00:31:13,009 --> 00:31:16,345
[ news anchor ] Just one night after a local teen was attacked in her home

556
00:31:16,478 --> 00:31:18,714
by an assailant wearing a Ghostface costume ,

557
00:31:18,848 --> 00:31:21,784
Sheriff Judy Hicks has now confirmed two more late-night attacks

558
00:31:21,918 --> 00:31:23,820
that have left Woodsboro reeling .

559
00:31:23,953 --> 00:31:25,587
The first victim , Vincent Schneider ,

560
00:31:25,721 --> 00:31:28,158
was found dead behind the Corner Pocket Pool Hall .

561
00:31:28,290 --> 00:31:30,126
A second victim , as yet unnamed ,

562
00:31:30,259 --> 00:31:34,430
was attacked inside Woodsboro General Hospital , but escaped without injuries .

563
00:31:34,563 --> 00:31:37,133
Needless to say , Woodsboro is on high alert today ...

564
00:31:37,266 --> 00:31:40,502
[ TV announcer ] Live from Studio 1-A in Rockefeller Plaza ...

565
00:31:40,636 --> 00:31:42,271
Good morning . I 'm Gale Weathers .

566
00:31:42,404 --> 00:31:45,674
Before we dive in , I want to tell you a little story

567
00:31:45,809 --> 00:31:48,377
that happened on the way into the studio this morning .

568
00:31:48,510 --> 00:31:50,679
- I stopped to get a bacon ... - [ knocking on door ]

569
00:31:50,814 --> 00:31:53,515
... at a bodega , already a quintessentially New York ...

570
00:31:53,649 --> 00:31:54,717
Go away !

571
00:31:54,851 --> 00:31:57,219
[ Sam ] Sorry to bother you , Mr. Riley !

572
00:31:57,352 --> 00:31:59,655
We just want to ask you a few questions .

573
00:32:00,355 --> 00:32:02,391
[ Dewey ] I don 't give interviews .

574
00:32:02,524 --> 00:32:03,927
We 're not looking for an interview .

575
00:32:04,060 --> 00:32:05,661
[ footsteps approaching ]

576
00:32:05,794 --> 00:32:07,763
Give me one good reason why I should talk to you .

577
00:32:07,897 --> 00:32:10,299
I 'm Billy Loomis 's daughter .

578
00:32:11,700 --> 00:32:14,369
That 's a terrible reason for me to talk to you .

579
00:32:15,071 --> 00:32:16,672
My name is Samantha Carpenter .

580
00:32:16,806 --> 00:32:18,808
I was attacked last night at the hospital .

581
00:32:18,942 --> 00:32:22,244
The night before that , my sister was stabbed seven times .

582
00:32:22,377 --> 00:32:23,947
I know you know what that 's like .

583
00:32:24,080 --> 00:32:25,247
[ sighs ]

584
00:32:25,380 --> 00:32:27,050
I 'm just trying to protect my family .

585
00:32:28,017 --> 00:32:30,954
Five minutes . That 's all I 'm asking .

586
00:32:33,189 --> 00:32:34,623
I 'll give you two minutes .

587
00:32:34,757 --> 00:32:36,291
I 'm missing a show I like .

588
00:32:36,425 --> 00:32:38,393
... bangs again , stage an intervention .

589
00:32:38,527 --> 00:32:39,996
[ Richie ] Gale Weathers .

590
00:32:40,130 --> 00:32:43,265
- Weren 't you two , um ... - Yeah .

591
00:32:52,142 --> 00:32:53,176
Who 's he ?

592
00:32:53,308 --> 00:32:55,377
Oh , this is Richie , my boyfriend .

593
00:32:55,511 --> 00:32:57,247
How long have you known him ?

594
00:32:57,379 --> 00:32:58,547
Six months ?

595
00:32:58,680 --> 00:33:00,917
Did he know who your dad was when you met ?

596
00:33:01,650 --> 00:33:03,318
Express any interest in Woodsboro

597
00:33:03,452 --> 00:33:05,420
or the Ghostface killings ?

598
00:33:05,554 --> 00:33:07,090
What the hell are you talking about ?

599
00:33:07,223 --> 00:33:09,993
Your killer 's obsessed with the Stab movies , right ?

600
00:33:10,126 --> 00:33:14,831
Well , there are certain rules to surviving a Stab movie .

601
00:33:15,999 --> 00:33:17,432
Believe me , I know .

602
00:33:18,333 --> 00:33:20,170
Rule number one :

603
00:33:20,302 --> 00:33:22,038
Never trust the love interest .

604
00:33:22,172 --> 00:33:25,507
They seem sweet , caring , supportive . Then welcome to act 3 ,

605
00:33:25,641 --> 00:33:26,943
where they 're trying to rip your head off .

606
00:33:27,076 --> 00:33:29,745
I was with Sam in Modesto when Tara was attacked .

607
00:33:29,879 --> 00:33:31,915
And let me guess , you were just in the other room ,

608
00:33:32,048 --> 00:33:35,185
conveniently unaccounted for when she was attacked at the hospital .

609
00:33:35,317 --> 00:33:38,654
Okay , do I have to take this from shitty Sam Elliott over here , or what ?

610
00:33:38,787 --> 00:33:41,157
- Rule number two ... - [ scoffs ]

611
00:33:41,291 --> 00:33:45,694
... the killer 's motive is always connected to something in the past .

612
00:33:46,762 --> 00:33:48,430
- I 'm related to Billy . - Right ,

613
00:33:48,564 --> 00:33:51,333
but then why kill that random Vince guy ?

614
00:33:51,466 --> 00:33:52,969
That 's for you to figure out .

615
00:33:53,102 --> 00:33:56,306
And rule number three , and this is the most important rule :

616
00:33:56,438 --> 00:34:01,110
The first victim always has a friend group that the killer is a part of .

617
00:34:02,111 --> 00:34:04,280
Does your sister have a close-knit group of friends ?

618
00:34:04,413 --> 00:34:05,882
Yeah .

619
00:34:07,283 --> 00:34:08,517
She does .

620
00:34:08,650 --> 00:34:10,352
Then look for the killer there .

621
00:34:11,221 --> 00:34:13,189
If you can find out why they 're doing this ,

622
00:34:13,323 --> 00:34:14,891
you can figure out who 's next .

623
00:34:15,925 --> 00:34:17,093
So help us .

624
00:34:17,927 --> 00:34:19,896
Help us figure out who is behind this .

625
00:34:20,029 --> 00:34:22,798
You kidding me ? I 've been stabbed nine times .

626
00:34:22,932 --> 00:34:25,400
I 've got permanent nerve damage and a fun little limp .

627
00:34:25,534 --> 00:34:27,469
You think I want to do that again ?

628
00:34:27,603 --> 00:34:31,440
You just said it always goes back to the past , right ?

629
00:34:32,708 --> 00:34:35,477
So if I 'm in danger ...

630
00:34:36,246 --> 00:34:37,981
that means you 're in danger .

631
00:34:39,148 --> 00:34:40,515
Come on .

632
00:34:40,649 --> 00:34:43,052
Let 's do this together .

633
00:34:46,189 --> 00:34:47,156
Your time 's up .

634
00:34:47,290 --> 00:34:48,690
- [ door slams ] - Jesus !

635
00:34:49,558 --> 00:34:50,726
[ sighs ]

636
00:34:50,860 --> 00:34:52,996
Yeah , he 's way more fun in the movies .

637
00:34:55,832 --> 00:34:57,499
Okay , uh , what 's next ?

638
00:34:57,633 --> 00:34:59,035
The friends .

639
00:35:00,702 --> 00:35:02,404
[ new anchor ] Thanks so much for that , Kevin .

640
00:35:02,537 --> 00:35:03,873
Coming up after our local weather ,

641
00:35:04,007 --> 00:35:06,910
the pros and cons of reuniting with old friends .

642
00:35:07,043 --> 00:35:08,443
[ TV clicks off ]

643
00:35:19,554 --> 00:35:21,024
[ sighs ]

644
00:35:29,265 --> 00:35:31,100
[ cell phone ringing ]

645
00:35:35,338 --> 00:35:36,505
Hello ?

646
00:35:36,638 --> 00:35:38,440
[ Dewey ] Hey , Sid , it 's me .

647
00:35:39,474 --> 00:35:40,944
Dewey ? [ chuckles ]

648
00:35:41,077 --> 00:35:43,478
Oh , my God . How long has it been ?

649
00:35:43,612 --> 00:35:46,349
I 'm just trying to get a run in before I take the girls to school .

650
00:35:46,481 --> 00:35:47,417
How are you ?

651
00:35:47,549 --> 00:35:49,419
I 'm good , really good .

652
00:35:49,551 --> 00:35:51,120
How are you ? How 's Mark ?

653
00:35:51,254 --> 00:35:52,721
I think I 'll keep him .

654
00:35:52,855 --> 00:35:54,656
How are things in the sheriff 's business ?

655
00:35:54,790 --> 00:35:56,392
Uh , they 're ...

656
00:35:56,525 --> 00:36:00,196
- They 're fine . But , Sid ... - Have you talked to Gale lately ?

657
00:36:01,797 --> 00:36:03,598
No . Not in a couple years .

658
00:36:03,732 --> 00:36:06,768
I know things didn 't end well with you guys , but ...

659
00:36:06,903 --> 00:36:07,971
Sid ...

660
00:36:08,537 --> 00:36:09,872
